clutched:
The hours slid fast, as hours will,
Clutched tight by greedy hands;
So faces on two decks look back,

clubs:
To enrich them? pray instruct me how it’s done.
First, clubs,—and while you look at clubs, it’s spades;
That’s prodigy. The lightning strikes a man,

clustered:
So the Prince was tended with care:
One wrung foul ooze from his clustered hair;
Two chafed his hands, and did not spare;

clustering:
Again, I feel her fingers glide
Amid my clustering hair;
I see the love-light in her eyes,

clues:
Through sly intricacies;
Ten thousand years on jungle clues
Alone shaped feet like these.

cluck:
Was stormed and forced by the full rout of day:
The rasp of a saw, the fussy cluck and bray
Of hens, the wheeze of a pump, she needs must hear;

With wary half-closed eyes;
The cock has ceased to crow, the hen to cluck:
Only the fox is out, some heedless duck

clumping:
